`iComp` is the m-th coordinate of the stage embedding of x. It climbs from x by the tower of inclusions when m is at least n, and descends from x by the tower of retractions when m is below n.

`iComp_of_le` is the climb, the branch taken when n is at most m. `iComp_of_ge` is the descent, the branch taken when m is below n. `iComp_self` is the coordinate at stage n: the climb from a stage to itself is the identity. `iComp_incl_le` says the embedding of the n-th coordinate of a thread lies below the thread at every coordinate. When the coordinate is later, climbing a coordinate of the thread stays below it. When the coordinate is earlier, descending a thread recovers that coordinate. `iComp_preservesDirectedSup` says each coordinate preserves directed suprema, because it is either the climb or the descent, and each of those does. `iComp_monotone` follows, since a map that preserves directed suprema is monotone. `iComp_compatible` says the resulting sequence is a thread. At a later coordinate both the current component and the next climb, one inclusion peels off, and a retraction after an inclusion is the identity. On the step where the stage is exactly one past the coordinate, the later component is the identity and the earlier one is one descent. When the stage is still later, both components descend and peeling the last retraction matches the shorter descent.
